{
  "category": "Dragon Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Long considered a mythical POKéMON until recently when a small colony was found living underwater.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long considered a mythical POKéMON until recently when a small colony was found living underwater.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "The existence of this mythical POKéMON was only recently confirmed by a fisherman who caught one.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is born large to start with. It repeatedly sheds its skin as it steadily grows longer.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON is full of life energy. It continually sheds its skin and grows steadily larger.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sheds many layers of skin as it grows larger. Dur ing this process, it is protected by a rapid waterfall.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "DRATINI continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "DRATINI continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A DRATINI continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even the young can exceed 6.5 feet in length. It grows larger by repeatedly shedding skin.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long considered a mythical POKéMON until recently, when a small colony was found living underwater.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is born large to start with. It repeatedly sheds its skin as it steadily grows longer.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is full of life energy. It continually sheds its skin and grows steadily larger.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is full of life energy. It continually sheds its skin and grows steadily larger.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dratini continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dratini continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It grows by molting repeatedly. Boots made from the tanned cast-off skin are a super luxury item.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a 10-hour struggle, a fisherman was able to pull one up and confirm its existence.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s still weak, so it lurks on the floor of bodies of water, eating whatever food sinks down and living a quiet life.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sheds its skin—almost on a daily basis—and grows larger. Its skin is soft just after it’s been shed.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long thought to be a myth, this Pokémon’s existence was only recently confirmed by a fisherman who caught one.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long thought to be a myth, this Pokémon’s existence was only recently confirmed by a fisherman who caught one.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dratini dwells near bodies of rapidly flowing water, such as the plunge pools of waterfalls. As it grows, Dratini will shed its skin many times.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon was long considered to be no more than a myth. The small lump on a Dratini’s forehead is actually a horn that’s still coming in.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
